\pard\f0\cf1\b\fs27 A. How to resume in a new chat\b0\cf0\fs22\sa100\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 Paste RESUME_PROMPT.md (RESUME_PROMPT.md) into a new session, or ask the agent to read docs/PROJECT_MEMORY.md and docs/MASTER_DEVELOPMENT_SPEC.md. Every session must:\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 1. Check the exact current main SHA, PRs, branches, workflows, dirty files and permissions. This snapshot can be stale.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 2. Read README.md, AGENTS.md, docs/INDEX.md, docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md and the actual code/tests before making a plan.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 3. Reuse tested functionality; select one narrow task, dependencies, test plan, security policy and rollback; no unnecessary infrastructure, models or rewrite.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 4. Implement on a focused branch, run actual tests, record pass/fail/skip, open PR, do not merge unreviewed work.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 5. Update this handbook, CHAT_CONTINUITY_LOG (CHAT_CONTINUITY_LOG.md), PROJECT_STATUS.md and a one-task handoff with commit/CI links. Exclude secrets, private judge cases, private submitted code and personal data from this public repo.\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\cf1\b\fs27 B. Project goals, product specification and honesty\b0\cf0\fs22\sa100\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 Primary learner journey: Pick an authorized original problem \u8594? read statement, samples and constraints \u8594? edit C++17/Python in Monaco \u8594? run sample cases \u8594? submit to isolated judge \u8594? see authentic AC/WA/CE/RE/TLE/MLE/OLE verdict \u8594? review owned history \u8594? read authored or authenticated hints \u8594? eventually obtain true AI tutoring, debugging and validated candidate-solving assistance.\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 Differentiation: Accessible progression from beginner to ICPC, grounded explanations, visible AI provenance, careful counterexample debugging, reproducible solver verification, personalization and affordable access. Competitors are workflow benchmarks, not code/content sources.\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
