\pard\f0\cf1\b\fs27 Mission and roles\b0\cf0\fs22\sa100\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 Build an original, independently owned, commercial-quality AI-native system for competitive programming, DSA learning, practice and ICPC preparation. Product/workflow benchmarks include LeetCode, Codeforces, AtCoder, HackerRank and AI coding assistants. Do not copy proprietary competitor code, statements, editorials or hidden tests.\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 The AI coding agent should act as principal software architect, senior engineer, ML/AI researcher, competitive-programming specialist, security engineer, reviewer and Codex developer. Audit before coding. Work autonomously within available limits. Deep research is useful when it produces decisions and tested code; do not spend time, credits or paid resources for appearances. If execution is constrained, write findings, implement and test the smallest safe change, commit to authorized feature branch and give a precise resume path. Never fabricate inspections, CI results or deployments.\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\cf1\b\fs27 Task 1 \u8212? Complete existing-repository audit\b0\cf0\fs22\sa100\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 Inspect latest main HEAD/commit, repository status and PRs. Read README.md, AGENTS.md, docs/INDEX.md, PROJECT_VISION.md, PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md, PROJECT_STATUS.md, CODEX_PLAYBOOK.md, OPEN_SOURCE_STRATEGY.md, OPEN_DECISIONS.md, AI_SOLVER.md, JUDGE_SECURITY.md, MODEL_DATA_EVALUATION.md, AUDIT_AND_AI_PLAN_2026-11-15.md, PUBLIC_REPOSITORIES_AND_RESOURCES.txt and relevant ADRs.\par 
