\pard\f0\cf1\b\fs27 Task 3 \u8212? Select exactly two AI problem-solving research references\b0\cf0\fs22\sa100\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 Previous selection: CodeSIM / MapCoder at https://github.com/kagnlp/CodeGenerator (planning, simulation and bounded refinement) plus phi-code at https://github.com/Nan-Do/phi-code (diverse candidates and tests-first ranking). Verify they remain best; change only if strongly justified. Record source modules, algorithms, synergy, integration plan, non-reusable code, security/license restrictions, complexity and measurable acceptance. Piston, DMOJ, MOJ and QingdaoU remain judge/contest references, not primary AI solvers. No unsupported benchmark claims.\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\cf1\b\fs27 Task 4 \u8212? Design the full incremental architecture\b0\cf0\fs22\sa100\par 
\pard\sa100\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - Frontend: professional accessible responsive Next.js; Monaco Python/C++, problem detail/samples, public authored hints, signed-in AI (when real), debugging, history, progress and eventual contests.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - Backend: preserve FastAPI and Better Auth/JWT ownership, queue and judge APIs; use narrow typed/versioned contracts, bounded inference orchestration; postpone DB/queue migration until measured.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - Tutor: explain algorithms from beginner to advanced, progressive non-spoiler hints, explain code/complexity, review solutions, analyze likely logic errors, track authorized learning progress, and label output authored / mock / model honestly.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - Debugger: reproduce only in authorized isolated execution, explain CE/RE/WA, show minimal fixes, use real evidence, redact hidden tests and privileged data.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - Verified solver: parse constraints, classify algorithm families, plan approaches, generate multiple bounded candidates, simulate/reason, compile and test in gVisor, rank by evidence, cap retries, explain proof ideas/complexity and uncertainty, track cost/latency/accuracy. Do not exec/eval/host subprocess arbitrary code; finite passed tests are not universal correctness proof.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - ICPC/contests: later registrations, teams, scoring/penalties, freeze, rating/analytics, administration, contest-integrity AI restrictions; not before essential learning/solver gates.\par 
\pard\f0\fs21\li0 - Models: provider-neutral offline mode, deterministic tests first; compare API and open-weight models separately; train/serve with Transformers/TRL/PEFT/Unsloth/vLLM only when legal data, benchmarks, economics, GPUs and approval justify it.\par 
